--- body ---
## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **High**

## Context
The README install step 2 gives:
```bash
curl -fsSL https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg/raw/2026-05-30/tickets/erg \
  -o tickets/erg && chmod +x tickets/erg
```
The date `2026-05-30` is the writing date, not a version tag. A user following
this README days or months later will either get a 404 (date doesn't exist as a
ref) or silently get a stale binary. There's no explanation of what the date
means or where to find a newer one.

## Fix
Use a stable URL. Options:
- `raw/main/tickets/erg` — always latest, no version pinning
- `gh release download` against a proper semver tag — explicit versioning

If the intent is security pinning (reproducible install), the date-as-ref model
needs an explanation and a pointer to where new release refs are announced.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] curl URL in README install step 2 uses a stable or well-explained ref
- [ ] A developer following the README 3 months from now gets a working binary
